<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="73fb2f79">The business analyst is responsible for eliciting the actual needs of stakeholders, not simply their expressed desires. In
many cases, the business analyst will also work to facilitate communication between organizational units. In particular,
business analysts often play a central role in aligning the needs of business units with the capabilities delivered by
information technology, and may serve as a “translator” between those groups.</attribute>
